course: dictionary
lesson: 4178
title: Golconda: a place and a treasure
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Golconda is a name you may meet in history lessons. «Until the 1700s almost all the world's diamonds came from India, from the Golconda region.» The capital G shows that Golconda is the name of one real place, so it is a proper noun.
explain: Golconda was an old fort and city ruin near Hyderabad in India, famous for its diamond mines. Because it was so rich in diamonds, people began to use golconda as an ordinary word for a source of great wealth, like a very rich mine.
explain: The small g is a clue. When golconda is not a place name, it is a common noun. Try the swap: «a golconda» becomes «a very rich mine». If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the meaning.
fact: Golconda is a proper noun when it is a place name, so it starts with a capital letter.
fact: «Golconda» (a place) is an old fort and city ruin near Hyderabad in India.
fact: «A golconda» (old, literary) means a source of great wealth, like a very rich mine.
fact: Golconda was famous for its diamond mines and its diamond trade.
fact: Some well-known diamonds, such as the Koh-i-Noor and the Hope Diamond, are believed to come from Golconda's mines.
exercise: «Until the 1700s almost all the world's diamonds came from India, from the Golconda region.» What is Golconda here? | A wise old king | A river in Scotland | *A place, an old fort and city ruin in India | A type of diamond cut
exercise: In an old book, a writer says «the bank vault was a golconda». What does golconda mean here? | A small wooden boat | *A source of great wealth, like a very rich mine | A kind of bird | A cold, dark cave
exercise: Which word starts with a capital letter because it is the name of a place? | diamond | *Golconda | mine | wealth
test: The famous painting by René Magritte is called Golconda, and it shows men in bowler hats falling like rain. What is Golconda in this sentence? | *The title of a famous painting | A kind of diamond | A fort in France | A rainy city in England
test: Why is Golconda famous in history lessons? | It was known for selling gold coins only | It was the first city to have cars | It was a famous football ground | *Its mines are linked to some world-famous diamonds
exam: Which meaning fits best in «The old gold mine was a golconda of wealth»? | A type of fish | Something with no value | A small village | *A source of great wealth, like a very rich mine
